  "notes": "Manifest says cash basis but the statements are GAAP (government-wide net position, modified accrual governmental funds, accrual proprietary funds); basis recorded as GAAP. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental column (p4). Taxes 8,817,578 split into sales tax (Sales Tax fund = SoA Sales 1,910,601) and property tax 6,906,977 (TIF fund by name; General and Bond by subtraction). Tax increment financing (4,353,191) and sale of property 74,279 are other financing sources/uses (other_financing). Prior period adjustment 272,039 (fund balances) in adjustments; the government-wide restatement (672,515, full accrual conversion) is in governmental_net_position. ending_cash = governmental funds Cash and investments 6,747,099 (p3); cash with County Treasurer 137,342 separate. Business-type from proprietary Total column (Utilities + Nursing Home, p6), spending by cost type with function utilities. Proprietary noncapital financing is the interfund activity line (111,590); it differs from the 1,586,127 transfers in the operating statement as printed. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (internal balances net to zero). Detail from the three budget-and-actual schedules (pp8-10): combined governmental funds excluding the Debt Service Fund, the Debt Service Fund, and the proprietary funds (budget basis). Read pages 1-10 of 10."
}
